   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 435 of the laws of 2014 amending the environmental\nconservation law relating to defining spearguns and allowing recreational\nspearfishing in New York's marine and coastal waters, in relation to extending\nthe effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S2724",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2724-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 435 of 2014",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2724\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 435 of the laws of 2014 amending the environ-\nmental conservation law relating to defining spearguns and allowing\nrecreational spearfishing in New York's marine and coastal waters, in\nrelation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the provisions of Chapter 435 of the Laws of 2014, which\nallows for recreational spearfishing in New York's marine and coastal\nwaters, for three years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Extends for three years the provisions of Section 3 of Chap-\nter 435 of the Laws of 2014 amending the Environmental Conservation Law\nrelating to defining spearguns and allowing recreational spearfishing in\nNew York's marine and coastal waters\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe current law which allows for recreational spearfishing in New York's\nmarine and coastal waters sunsets on June 1, 2020. This legislation is\nnecessary to extend the effectiveness of this law for an additional\nthree years to June 1, 2024.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSenate\n\n2019-2020: S8094, Referred to Environmental Conservation\n\n2021-2022:  S4251, Passed Senate\n\nAssembly\n\n2019-2020: A10147, Referred to environmental conservation\n\n2021-2022:  No Assembly Same-As\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
